# Citation File Format (CFF) v1.2.0 https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# GitHub auto-renders this in the "Cite this repository" widget.
# Zenodo reads it during release-to-DOI minting.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use uncorrupt to clean or audit a scientific spreadsheet, please cite the canonical Ziemann papers AND this tool."
title: "UnCorrupt (uncorrupt): Detection and prevention of Excel-style gene-symbol corruption in scientific spreadsheets"
abstract: >-
  Detects and reverses Excel auto-conversion damage in supplementary
  spreadsheets accompanying genomics papers: gene symbols converted to
  dates (SEPT7 -> Sep-07), RIKEN/accession IDs coerced to floats
  (2310009E13 -> 2.31E+19), leading zeros stripped, and the rest of
  the Excel pathology documented by Ziemann et al. (2016, 2021). The
  detector reaches 95.16 % cell-level recall (1591/1672 verifiable
  cells) against an EPMC-expanded extension of Ziemann's 2021 S2
  corpus (re-verified 2026-05-25), 100 % recall on the older Ziemann
  2016 corpus (279/279 files), and 100 % post-boost precision at all
  user-facing confidence levels (>= 0.50) against 2,180 xref-validated
  positive cells. Replication scan covered 19,500 supplementary files
  across 11 high-impact genetics journals (2022-2026); detector flagged
  high-confidence corruption in 988 distinct papers. Emits a
  Frictionless Table Schema sidecar that prevents future corruption
  on import.
